{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-08T21:56:33.018Z","data":{"text":"Both verifies pass. Task 7 is complete.\n\n**Summary of what I did:**\n\n1. **`contracts.ts`** — re-exports `ApprovalNotices`, `ApprovalNotice`, `NoticeSeverity` as types only from `src/core/spec/notices.ts`.\n\n2. **New `NoticePanel.tsx`** — renders the notice block: `Notices` h3, `Nothing unusual` when `unusual` is false, one `<details>` per shown notice (severity word + label in the summary, detail below), and one `<details>` summarised `<k> more` holding the rest. Each notice's `onToggle` calls `onOpen(id)`.\n\n3. **New `notice-state.ts`** — `unopenedRedLabels(notices, opened)` returns the labels of unopened red notices in notice order; `approveInput(opened)` returns `{ verb: 'approve', opened }` sorted, or `{ verb: 'approve' }` when `opened` is undefined. `WebActionInput`'s approve member gained `opened?: readonly string[]`.\n\n4. **`ChangeView.tsx`** — keeps opened ids in state, renders `NoticePanel` after the header/error and before the brief for a review with notices, and threads opened ids + unopened red labels into `ChangeActionsPanel`, which posts `approveInput(opened)`.\n\n5. **`ChangeActions.tsx`** — optional `approveBlockedBy` disables Approve and shows `Open each red notice to approve: <label>, <label>`.\n\n6. **New `notices.css`** (imported by `main.tsx` next to `review.css`) — stripe classes using the dashboard's `--status-*` tokens and `overflow-wrap: anywhere`.\n\n7. **New `tests/ui-notices.test.tsx`** (245 lines) — covers every \"Notice block view\" scenario via `renderToStaticMarkup`, pure helpers, CSS checks, and a real `getWebChange` document.\n\nAll within scope; `pnpm verify` (proposal verify) and the task verify both pass."}}
